  "path": "straight cardinal ray starting at the missing border pixel and continuing outward perpendicular to that side until the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "paint the missing border pixel and every background pixel on the ray red",
  "transform": "also fill s's 2x2 interior red; preserve all frame pixels and unrelated background"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 7-11 rows x 9-15 cols
  background: any color except blue (1) and red (2)
  frames:
    count: 1-3
    shape: 4x4 rectangular border (12 border cells) with exactly 1 non-corner pixel removed, giving area 11
    color: always blue (1) [observed]
    gap_offset: 1 or 2 along the side (never corner); any of the 4 sides
    gap_side: top, bottom, left, or right (all 4 observed)
  ray:
    direction: outward perpendicular from gap side to grid edge
    length: 0-3 cells beyond the gap pixel (gap pixel itself is also painted)
    content: ray passes only through background pixels, never through another frame
  placement:
    frames do not overlap and their 4x4 bboxes are separated by >=1 cell in at least one axis
    rays must not intersect any frame pixel
  output_transform:
    fill each frame's 2x2 interior with red (2)
    fill the gap pixel with red (2)
    extend a red ray from the gap outward to grid edge (all bg pixels along the ray become red)

generation_strategy:
  approach: place frames then verify rays
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H in [7..15], W in [7..15], ensuring room for 1-3 frames
    2. Pick bg color from {0,3,4,5,6,7,8,9} (not blue/red), frame color = blue (1)
    3. Pick N frames in [1..3]
    4. For each frame, pick a random gap side and gap offset (1 or 2)
    5. Place frames on the grid greedily, ensuring 4x4 bboxes do not overlap (>=1 cell gap)
    6. For each frame, compute the ray from gap outward; verify it hits only bg pixels (no other frame)
    7. If ray collision detected, retry placement; rejection rate is low with >=1 cell separation
    8. Build output by filling interiors + gap pixels + rays with red
